/**
@example hello_world/hello_world.cpp
The smallest app: a window, a text field and buttons, and the program around them.
Walkthrough: @ref md_docs_2examples_2hello-world "Hello world".

@example controls/controls.cpp
The common controls as label/value rows: buttons, toggles, text and number fields, a
slider, a color, a menu and tabs.
Walkthrough: @ref md_docs_2examples_2controls "Controls".

@example docking/docking.cpp
Panels in a dock layout that the user can rearrange, tear off and dock again.
Walkthrough: @ref md_docs_2examples_2docking "Docking".

@example custom_theme/custom_theme.cpp
Your own CSS classes next to the library's, and switching palettes and font size at
runtime. Its classes are in custom_theme.css.
Walkthrough: @ref md_docs_2examples_2custom-theme "Custom theme".

@example custom_theme/custom_theme.css
The custom_theme example's own CSS classes.

@example host_device/host_device.cpp
Running on a Vulkan device the application already owns, and showing an image it renders.
Walkthrough: @ref md_docs_2examples_2host-device "Host device".
*/
